# The working tree is LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# `.prettierrc` sets no `endOfLine`, so prettier defaults to `lf`. Without this file a checkout on
# Windows (`core.autocrlf=true`) materialises CRLF, and the pre-push `format:check` then fails on 82
# files nobody touched - a gate reporting the operating system rather than the code. The blobs were
# already LF, so this changes no committed content: it fixes what a checkout writes to disk.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never normalised, or they are corrupted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
